  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Implementing the Conservation and Management Strategy for the Black Rhino in Kenya 2017-2021</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Five conservancies (Borana, Ol Jogi, Lewa, Ol Pejeta and Solio) in Laikipia County in northern Kenya contain a significant portion of Kenyas total black rhino population and collaborate under the umbrella of the Association of Private Land Rhino Sanctuaries. At the request of Kenya Wildlife Service (KWS), these funds will support the employment of an Administrator to work alongside the KWS Rhino Program Coordinator in order to better coordinate information and management activities among the conservancies and in support of Kenyas national rhino management objectives.</narrative>
  </description>
